Mobile: pinch-zoom, responsive UI, perf tuning

- CameraRig: track multi-touch pointers, two-finger pinch -> FOV; drag
  sensitivity now scales with current FOV so a swipe at 12 deg feels the
  same as at 90 deg. Block native pinch/pull-to-refresh on the canvas.
- Hover: ignore non-mouse pointers (touch/pen-with-finger) so labels
  don't flicker mid-drag. Sun & Planets gate hover by pointerType too.
- Scene: detect coarse pointer / <768px and downshift DPR cap to 1.5,
  Milky Way to 64x32 segments, anisotropy to 4, bloom radius/intensity
  slightly tighter on phones.
- MilkyWay: accept a quality prop ("low" | "high").
- page.tsx: full mobile-first layout. Compact header, full-width
  SignReveal at top, ApodCard hidden under md, ObjectInfoPanel becomes
  a bottom sheet on phones, bottom dock stacks vertically with
  DateScrubber bottom-most for thumb reach.
- DateScrubber: 36px+ tap targets, full-width on mobile.
- LayerToggles: collapses behind a 40px icon button on phones.
- ZoomControls: horizontal row on mobile w/ 40px hit areas.
- SearchPalette: icon-only button on phones, full-width modal,
  larger 16px input to suppress iOS auto-zoom on focus, autocorrect off.
- HelpHint: switches text to "Drag / Pinch / Tap" on coarse pointers.
- globals.css: lock html, disable overscroll/pull-to-refresh, add
  safe-area inset utilities, body uses touch-action: manipulation.
- viewport: minimumScale=1, userScalable=false (we manage zoom).
